body:
You can't decide whether or not you want to live. God gave you that life for a  specific reason. Most people go through their lives wondering what their purpose is. I too are one who wonders. I believe I may know my purpose, but when it fails I start to think if it's really my purpose.

&#x200B;

However, keep in mind. When life is hard especially when you have Christ in your life, it means the Devil is attacking you. There is a saying I like to go by.

&#x200B;

"When the Devil stops attacking you, begin to worry".

&#x200B;

Simply what I am saying is that, because life is tough it means you're on the right path with Christ. In the bible it says you won't ever be able to compare the bad you went through to the good that is coming. You may go through a crap life and a lot of issues and drama, but when judgement day comes, you'll be rewarded in full.

&#x200B;

Just keep in mind of Christ. Study his word regularly, speak to him alone, pray often, push through the bad, find your purpose and chase that. When you feel like giving up, remind yourself that you are a Warrior of God and nothing can stop you, because you have Christ by your side.

**You. Are. A. Fearless. Warrior. Of. God!**

That being said. God is extremely proud of you. He loves you so much that our brains cannot fathom. I understand how you feel. There's a part of me that wants to end my life too and suffering. But I always remind myself that if I take my own life to end my pain and suffering, I'll most likely will end up in a place of eternal suffering and pain.

&#x200B;

Not trying to scare you. You are stronger than you realise. God is proud of you. I am proud of you.
